Follow-up from B359 (which deliberately skipped the forward-agent-log muse classifier): muse session.jsonl is a transaction-frame log, not a role/content line stream. Measured on-host (2026-10-02): first-line top-level keys are [children, content_sha256, frame_schema_version, outer_log_ordinal, retained_frame, transaction_id]; retained_frame is a string tag (e.g. session_permission_transaction) or null. None of the existing classify_*_line shapes fit. Work: design + prove a classify_muse_line over the retained_frame schema (measure 2+ real sessions, pin shapes in tests), add detect_format_by_path arm (muse sessions dir) + sniff arm (frame_schema_version/transaction_id keys), extend supported_formats + --format docs. Guard: an unproven sniff must fail closed (None), never misclassify another client's transcript as muse.

Coordinator decision: DEFERRED out of the muse batch (low priority, 3h, standalone classifier work; B359 deliberately skipped it). Keep pending for a later slice; no dependency on B351 close.

Coordinator decision (bl-fix-many batch, 2026-10-04): Lane C, parallel — this IS the later slice the deferral note waited for (B351 now done; standalone classifier work, no dependency). Disjoint files (ocaml/cli/c2c_forward_agent_log*.ml). Verified still missing: supported_formats has no muse arm. Real muse sessions exist on host under ~/.local/share/muse/sessions/2026 for the 2-session measurement.